id1167064953114"><div data-type="title">Discussion</div>
<p id="fs-id1167065788791">This means that the two sound intensity levels differ by 3.01 dB, or about 3 dB, as advertised. Note that because only the ratio <em data-effect="italics">I</em><sub>2</sub>/<em data-effect="italics">I</em><sub>1</sub> is given (and not the actual intensities), this result is true for any intensities that differ by a factor of two. For example, a 56.0 dB sound is twice as intense as a 53.0 dB sound, a 97.0 dB sound is half as intense as a 100 dB sound, and so on.</p>
</div>
</section></div>
</div></section></div></section>



